Package: MIRTH
Type: Package
Title: Multiple Imputation for Removing Technical Heterogeneity
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Noah", "Hillman", email = "Noah.Hillman@pennmedicine.upenn.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Integrates ComBat-style harmonization of multi-site imaging
    features into machine-learning pipelines. The
    harmonization model is fit on training data and applied to the held-out test set when generating predictions. Outcomes (and any missing
    covariates) in new data are multiply imputed with 'mice', with each imputed data
    set being harmonized with the training-set batch-effect estimates. Predictions from a 'caret' model are generated on each imputed data set and pooled across imputations. Supports
    continuous, binary, and multi-class outcomes, and user-supplied harmonization methods. Options for harmonizing data with unseen sites in the test set are experimental and should be 
    performed cautiously. 
